  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.8.0 - Kuwantima: one new icon (Icon.Grid). Kuwantima.DataGrid: first release.\n\nIcon.Grid (Material Design Icons' view-grid, matching the existing MDI set) joins the icon set for the new DataGrid companion package's nav glyph, filling the one gap in the existing 14 that didn't read as a grid/table icon. 15 icons now ship, up from 14. Nothing else in the core package changed this release - no controls added, removed, or renamed. Control count stays 16.\n\nThe real news this release is Kuwantima.DataGrid, a new companion package styling Avalonia's DataGrid control (Avalonia.Controls.DataGrid). It ships separately, as its own `dotnet add package`, because that control lives in its own Avalonia package, not core Avalonia - folding it into Kuwantima would force that dependency on every consumer, even ones who never use a grid. See the Kuwantima.DataGrid package's own release notes, and README's \"DataGrid (optional)\" section, for what it covers.\n\nBoth packages are versioned in lockstep (same number, same tag) even though only one of them has code changes beyond a single icon - see CLAUDE.md's Version Management section for why.",
